Every file in this folder is SYNTHETIC: written by hand for these tests in the
shape of each publisher's payload (FRED/ALFRED JSON, BLS v2 JSON, BEA NIPA JSON,
SEC EDGAR submissions, company facts, filing indexes, Form 4/144 XML, 13F
information tables and cover pages, N-PORT documents and the EDGAR browse feed,
the Federal Reserve's FOMC calendar and statements, NY Fed JSON, Treasury CSV,
FiscalData JSON, Nasdaq calendar JSON, NYSE, SIFMA and OPM holiday pages).

No file is a recording of a live response, and no value is real: the companies
(TESTCO, OTHRCO, LOSSCO), the managers (CIKs 9999950 and 9999951), the fund (series
S000099991, TFUND), every CIK, CUSIP, accession number, name, figure and
statement are invented. Structured files carry "_synthetic": true where the
format allows it; the SEC ticker lists cannot (their shape has no room for a
marker) and are listed here instead: sec.company_tickers.json and
sec.company_tickers_mf.json. Page fixtures say "synthetic" in a comment.

No key appears anywhere: the tests use the obvious fakes in data_harness.KEYS.
